Every clinician can possibly need a combined-immediate-release-and-ER-LA-opioid-prescription.
If a clinician prescribes an immediate-release-opioid with an ER-LA-opioid then the clinician should consider an increased-combination-overdose-risk and should prescribe the immediate-release-opioid with the ER-LA-opioid cautiously.
An immediate-release-and-ER-LA-opioid-combination-example includes an ER-LA-to-immediate-release-transition-example and includes a temporary-postoperative-short-term-opioid-use-example and includes a methadone-stabilized-patient-acute-pain-example.
Every combined-immediate-release-and-ER-LA-opioid-prescription can possibly increase an overdose-risk.
